= Agent self-identity — Simple =

'''Agent self-identity''' means keeping track of which persistent AI agent is the same agent across different runs.

An agent might restart, switch models, move to another machine, or begin a new session. Its persistent identity answers questions like:

* Which memories belong to it?
* Which goals and rules still apply?
* Which permissions does it have?
* Which past actions were its actions?

This is different from a username, API key, persona, or running process.

A credential can change while the agent remains the same agent. Two agents can also start from identical copied state while still being two different agents.

Agent self-identity is an engineering concept about continuity. It does not mean the agent is conscious.

